---
import VisualFigure from "./VisualFigure.astro";
---

<VisualFigure
  id="safapac-delivery"
  label="02 · Delivery"
  title="How SAFAPAC gets delivered"
  tone="safapac"
  altText="A compact SAFAPAC delivery path connects a web app through HTTPS and Nginx to a FastAPI backend and PostgreSQL. Docker, CI, AWS, and authentication form a supporting platform layer, with beta delivery as the outcome."
  caption="High-level web-to-data delivery within Hydar's SAFAPAC backend, database, and AWS scope."
>
  <div slot="graphic" class="visual-art visual-art--safapac-delivery" aria-hidden="true">
    <p class="v4d-label">Delivery path</p>

    <div class="v4d-delivery__path">
      <article class="v4d-delivery__node">
        <strong>Web app</strong>
      </article>
      <span class="v4d-delivery__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <article class="v4d-delivery__node">
        <strong>HTTPS / Nginx</strong>
      </article>
      <span class="v4d-delivery__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <article class="v4d-delivery__node">
        <strong>FastAPI</strong>
      </article>
      <span class="v4d-delivery__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <article class="v4d-delivery__node">
        <strong>PostgreSQL</strong>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="v4d-platform">
      <p class="v4d-label">Supports</p>
      <div class="v4d-platform__items">
        <span>Docker</span>
        <span>CI</span>
        <span>AWS</span>
        <span>Auth</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
  <ol slot="fallback" class="visual-figure__fallback-list">
    <li>The web app connects through HTTPS and Nginx to FastAPI.</li>
    <li>FastAPI reads and writes PostgreSQL data.</li>
    <li>Docker, CI, AWS, and authentication support the delivery path as a platform layer.</li>
  </ol>
</VisualFigure>
